# ── Backtest factor cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# During a backtest each bar hands the strategy a trailing window, so factors are
# recomputed from scratch every bar (81% of backtest time in profiling). The cache
# in core/factors_ts/cache.py computes each factor once over the full frame and
# serves windows as slices, but only for factors whose cached value matches the
# uncached one.
#
# Default 0 = bit-exact: only factors that come out bit-identical are cached.
# Computing over the full series instead of a 200-bar window leaves ~1e-11 of
# float noise in some factors, which is harmless until a strategy does
# `score > enter_th` and the epsilon flips a trade.
#
# Relaxing to 1e-9 caches more factors and is faster, at the cost of that drift.
# Measured on an 8-trial MultiFactorHF sweep over 3,000 bars:
#   0     (default) 1.40x, position series unchanged
#   1e-9            2.64x, position differed on 8 bars
# Use the relaxed setting for parameter sweeps and research, not for numbers you
# intend to trade on.
FACTOR_CACHE_REL_TOL=0
